# Mode 1: "Create a token that's a copy of target creature you control, except it's not legendary and it's a 4/4 Hero in addition to its other
# types" (CR 707.2, 707.9b, 111.1). Bot1's Ty Lee, Chi Blocker (a legendary 2/1 Human Performer Ally) is copied: the token is a 4/4 Hero Ally Human
# Performer, and since it is not legendary the legend rule (CR 704.5j) leaves both on the battlefield; the original stays a legendary 2/1 - a 3/2 until end of turn, its prowess having triggered on the Production (CR 702.108a), as the token that did not yet exist did not. The
# token's own enters trigger (the ruling: the copy's enters abilities trigger) is asked for a target, and Bot1 chooses none. An opponent's
# Memnite and Bot1's own Mox Pearl (not a creature) are refused as targets of this mode.

